  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1138 AM CST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\nThe upper low will transition to a broad open wave trough by Tuesday \nas it begins to move over the ArkLaTex region before being little \nmore than a subtle shortwave over the Southeast CONUS Wednesday. \nUpper ridging will build over the western CONUS during this time as \na progressive shortwave trough pushes a cold front southward across \nthe Northern and Central Plains. This front will only bring slightly \ncooler temperatures to the region as the airmass will be highly \nmodified due to a lack of surface snowpack across the northern \nCONUS. The front, along with northerly upper flow, will help to keep \nafternoon highs in the low to mid 60s through late week before upper \nridging begins to move overhead by the late weekend.",
